cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RootQuant-V2, please cite the accompanying paper (arXiv:2609.25567)."
title: "RootQuant-V2: Foundation-Model Root-Trait Regression from Minirhizotron Imagery"
abstract: >-
  RootQuant-V2 regresses living root length (mm) and surface area (mm2) directly
  from single RGB minirhizotron frames, with no segmentation labels. A frozen
  DINOv3 ViT-L/16 backbone is adapted with DoRA on the attention projections and
  a Mona multi-scale convolutional adapter on the MLP branch, read out by a
  learnable pool fused with a density-style extensive head. 11.9M trainable
  parameters (3.78% of the model). This repository distributes the source code
  and the trained weights; the dataset is not included.
